From b74f82b74f047c3c9ad9fb605862527752c58954 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 09:57:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0078 -- structured startup-phase timing
 report

WHY: this session's own real-hardware step-2 investigation scavenged a
single isolated log line (DOS-PORT room_transition t_ms=38960) and a
one-off Debug::Printf (6.37s single-view precache) by hand from raw
STDOUT.TXT to build a load-time hypothesis. That does not scale across
rig rounds and cannot be parsed automatically. This patch turns those
into one grep-able, RUNMANIFEST-style structured block plus an
aggregate precache summary, following the exact source-read discipline
this hub's own rules require (every phase boundary below was found by
reading initialize_engine()'s and load_game_file()'s own call order,
not guessed).

WHAT: a new DosPortStartupTiming struct (Engine/main/
dos_port_startup_timing.h), one shared instance (main.cpp), populated
by uclock()-ms brackets placed at the real phase boundaries:

- subsystem_init: engine_init_fonts()..engine_init_debug()
  (main/engine.cpp)
- gamedata_asset_load: load_game_file()'s own
  OpenMainGameFileFromDefaultAsset+ReadGameData..TryLoadGameScripts
  span (main/game_file.cpp) -- CLIB/asset index + game data parse
- script_vm_init: load_game_file()'s own InitGameState() call, which is
  where create_game_scripts() (script/script.cpp) actually instantiates
  the compiled script modules/global script/dialog script into the VM
- gfxmode_init: engine_try_set_gfxmode_any() (main/engine.cpp) -- a
  real, distinct cost found reading source, not in the milestone's
  originally-named phase list but a real step worth its own field
- sprite_index_init: engine_init_sprites() (main/engine.cpp)
- sprite_precache: just the cursor/player-view precache_view() span
  inside engine_init_game_settings() (main/engine.cpp), not that whole
  (larger, mostly unrelated) function
- first_room_load: the true first room, whichever of two real call
  paths reaches it first -- game_start.cpp's own direct load_new_room()
  call (the actual first-ever room, confirmed live: Trilby's Notes'
  STDOUT.TXT shows "Loading room 1" with no preceding "Room change
  requested to room 1", proving new_room() is NOT called for the first
  room) or, for a later in-game transition that happens to be the first
  one instrumented, new_room()'s own entry (ac/room.cpp). This is a
  real, previously-unverified gap in patch 0042's own commit message
  ("For room 1 ... this same pair doubles as the boot-to-first-frame
  load-time metric") -- that claim was never actually true for the
  literal first room; only the AfterFadein "ready" side (event.cpp)
  fired for it. Fixed as part of this patch since it shares the exact
  same instrumentation point.

precache_view()'s own already-computed per-call cost (ac/game.cpp) is
folded into a running aggregate (call count, frame count, slowest 3 by
total ms) instead of only being printed once and discarded.

The full block is emitted once, at the first room's own AfterFadein
"ready" event (ac/event.cpp) -- the same "first interactive frame"
point patch 0042 already established, not a new one:

  [DOS-PORT-STARTUP-BEGIN]
  schema_version=1
  subsystem_init_ms=<n>
  gamedata_asset_load_ms=<n>
  script_vm_init_ms=<n>
  gfxmode_init_ms=<n>
  sprite_index_init_ms=<n>
  sprite_precache_ms=<n>
  sprite_precache_view_count=<n>
  sprite_precache_frame_count=<n>
  sprite_precache_slowestN_view=<n> sprite_precache_slowestN_ms=<n>  (x3)
  first_room_load_ms=<n>
  total_to_first_frame_ms=<n>
  [DOS-PORT-STARTUP-END]

Honesty note: the named phases do NOT sum to total_to_first_frame_ms --
confirmed on a real DOSBox-X run (Trilby's Notes: phases sum ~3.1s,
total 4.45s). The ~1.3s gap is real, unaccounted-for time in engine
steps this patch deliberately did not instrument (backend init, disk
space/font checks, rotation settings, window setup,
engine_prepare_to_start_game()) -- named here rather than silently
absorbed into a neighboring phase, so a future round knows there is
still a real gap to close, not a complete accounting.

Also bridges DOSAGS_FLIP_INSTR=1 (this port's own DOSAGS_* naming, main.cpp)
to SDL_HINT_DOS_FLIP_INSTR (patch 0035, vendor/SDL's own per-flip timing
instrumentation, previously reachable only via the raw SDL env var name)
via a plain setenv() -- patch 0035's own read is a bare getenv(), not
through SDL_SetHint()'s registry, so this needed no SDL-side change.
Off by default, same as the flag it bridges to (a real per-flip cost
once enabled, per patch 0035's own comment).

VALIDATED on DOSBox-X against three real games spanning all three
depths and non-1 starting rooms (Trilby's Notes room 1, Maniac Mansion
Deluxe room 50, Shards of God room 0): all three phases sum sanely,
first_room_load_ms is non-negative for all three (confirming the
load_new_room() fix), and Shards' own sprite_precache_frame_count=68
matches the pre-existing Debug::Printf's own "68 frames" from the same
call, a real, independent cross-check. DOSAGS_FLIP_INSTR=1 confirmed to
activate patch 0035's own SDLDBG.LOG output (uwfb-stat/flip-instr-
counters lines) on a real run; confirmed OFF (zero such lines) when
unset. port_game.py validate's existing gate re-run clean (pass=true,
no regression) against trilbysnotes sound_off.

NOT exercised on real hardware this round -- DOSBox-X timings above are
mechanism confirmation only, per this hub's own dosbox_not_perf_proxy
rule; real numbers are a separate, later step for the operator to
schedule rig time against.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
